+    // device/vivo/1907N: when the AP interface is a freshly, dynamically created one (this
+    // device's dual-interface concurrent STA+AP wifi mode creates a brand new "wlanN" netdev
+    // per SoftAp session, instead of reusing the always-present "wlan0"), this device's
+    // Tethering process never receives netd's own interfaceAdded notification for it at all -
+    // confirmed via logcat across many attempts: "AddSingleAccessPoint, iface=wlan2"
+    // immediately followed by "Tried to Tether an unknown iface: wlan2", with no amount of
+    // waiting (tried up to several seconds) ever making mTetherStates learn about it.
+    // Meanwhile netd itself is fully aware of the interface the whole time (confirmed via
+    // "netd: interfaceGetCfg(wlan2)" succeeding on every attempt) - only the push
+    // notification to this process is missing, not netd's own knowledge of the interface.
+    // Rather than wait for a notification that may never arrive, register the interface
+    // directly here (mirroring exactly what interfaceAdded()/processInterfaceStateChange()
+    // would have done) whenever WifiService asks to tether an iface we don't know about yet.
+    // The newly created IpServer still needs a moment to run its own state machine up to
+    // STATE_AVAILABLE before tether() will accept it, so poll briefly for that (this wait is
+    // local/in-process, unlike the netd notification, so it's expected to resolve quickly).
+    private static final int TETHER_IFACE_AVAILABLE_MAX_RETRIES = 20;
+    private static final int TETHER_IFACE_AVAILABLE_RETRY_DELAY_MS = 50;
